als (T1, T3, T9). Discarding T5 leaves the T suit's terminals intact, which might be better for future plays. \n\nSo the answer is to play T5.\n", "output": "Evaluation: The best move is to discard T5 to maximize the chances of forming a Seven Pairs hand or All Terminals and Honors by removing a non-terminal tile.\nReason: Discarding T5 (a middle tile) reduces the hand's reliance on non-terminal tiles, preserving terminals (W1, W9, T1, T3, T9, B9) and honor tiles (F1, J3). This setup increases the likelihood of drawing a tile to complete a pair or achieve All Terminals and Honors if other non-terminals (B3) are later discarded. T5 is less critical for terminal-based patterns compared to other tiles.\nAnswer: Play T5"}
